# Shemá — prayer wall and Prayer Pulse (BE-09 · OBT-398)
#
# The wall is every request the teams authorized to be shared with the intercessor network,
# inside the caller's region scope; the Pulse is the same list as a text file for the network.
#
# Three things to know before running anything below:
#   * a request reaches either one only when it is authorized — the project's own request with
#     `prayerVisibility: "rede"`, a need with `prayerShared: true`. NULL is `coordenacao`;
#   * a project in a sensitive country comes back with `country: ""`, `base: ""` and
#     `locationWithheld: true` for every role, and the Pulse names its region instead;
#   * the Pulse is `resourceCircle`'s — any other role is refused with 403.
#
# Before running: seed the app and its roles, grant one, and give the account a region.
#   uv run python scripts/seed_apps_roles.py
#   uv run python scripts/grant_app_role.py circulo.local@test.com shema resourceCircle

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@accessToken = {{shema_login.response.body.tokens.access_token}}

### Login — named, so every request below reuses the token
# @name shema_login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "circulo.local@test.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### The wall — FE-44 §9.6's PrayerRequest[], newest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/requests
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The Prayer Pulse, in Portuguese — a text file, saved as pulso-de-oracao-<day>.txt
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/pulse
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### The Prayer Pulse, in English
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/shema/prayer/pulse?lang=en
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
